# AWS Cloud Migration Checklist

A practical, no-fluff checklist for teams planning a migration to AWS — covering assessment, planning, execution, and post-migration validation. Built from real-world migration engagements by [Sygitech](https://sygitech.com).

## Why this exists

Most migration guides are either too generic (marketing content) or too narrow (one specific tool). This repo is a working checklist you can actually follow, fork, and adapt to your own environment.

## What's inside

- **Pre-migration assessment** — application inventory, dependency mapping, licensing checks
- **Strategy selection** — lift-and-shift vs. re-platform vs. re-architect (6 R's decision guide)
- **Cost estimation** — how to size instances and estimate AWS spend before you move
- **Migration execution** — cutover planning, data sync strategies, rollback plans
- **Post-migration validation** — performance baselines, cost monitoring, security review
- **Common pitfalls** — mistakes we've seen teams make repeatedly, and how to avoid them

## Who this is for

DevOps engineers, cloud architects, and IT leads planning or executing an AWS migration — whether it's your first workload or your fiftieth.

## Usage

Clone this repo and use `checklist.md` as a working document during your migration project. Check items off, add your own environment-specific notes, and adapt the phases to your timeline.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/sygitech/aws-cloud-migration-checklist.git
```

